Ummm!  I think that the quantifiers behave differently for 'lo' and 'loi'  =
're lo ci gerku' is two of the three dogs acting individually but 're loi c=
i gerku' is a bunch of two, i.e., acting still together.  There's something=
 about fractional quantifiers as well, but I am even less sure how that wor=
ks: 'pire lo'i gerku' is maybe halves of dogs for 'lo' but, I think, still =
a bunch of dogs half the original size for 'loi'.



